WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.075
Odin Close Control is an independent concept by Ayo Ahmed.

2
00:00:04.075 --> 00:00:11.115
This synthetic demonstration turns close preparation into an inspectable path: cash. evidence. then an explicit

3
00:00:11.115 --> 00:00:12.485
human review.

4
00:00:12.585 --> 00:00:18.789
I select both CSV files and confirm the synthetic-only scope.

5
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.005
I upload commitments and payment events together.

6
00:00:22.005 --> 00:00:25.840
The server validates exact amounts and previews the changes.

7
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.295
Both files are applied atomically to this saved session.

8
00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:33.155
I apply both files as one validated import.

9
00:00:33.274 --> 00:00:37.429
Aurora still has a two thousand pound receipt without an allocation.

10
00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:42.164
A receipt does not become funded capital until a human assigns it to the correct

11
00:00:42.164 --> 00:00:43.114
commitment.

12
00:00:43.214 --> 00:00:47.579
I open the receipt and select Linden's commitment.

13
00:00:47.704 --> 00:00:51.244
I select Linden Ventures for this two thousand pound receipt.

14
00:00:51.244 --> 00:00:54.614
The account. amount and bank reference stay visible.

15
00:00:54.614 --> 00:00:57.249
The selection becomes part of the audit trail.

16
00:00:57.349 --> 00:01:01.949
I explicitly confirm this receipt's known commitment account.

17
00:01:02.063 --> 00:01:04.553
The principal now reconciles.

18
00:01:04.553 --> 00:01:08.668
The fee cash is tracked separately using an illustrative fee rule.

19
00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:12.003
A draft legal reference still blocks a review request.

20
00:01:12.103 --> 00:01:14.104
Next. the final synthetic reference.

21
00:01:14.204 --> 00:01:18.124
I attach final synthetic legal metadata with a document hash.

22
00:01:18.124 --> 00:01:20.624
This records a human supplied reference.

23
00:01:20.624 --> 00:01:24.484
It does not verify a real agreement or replace legal judgment.

24
00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.622
I attach the final metadata.

25
00:01:27.745 --> 00:01:30.700
Every deterministic blocker is resolved.

26
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.010
Human attestations and the close request are present.

27
00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.485
The preparer can now request review of this exact revision.

28
00:01:37.585 --> 00:01:41.518
I request review and open this snapshot.

29
00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:46.284
The synthetic reviewer inspects the current revision and explicitly confirms it.

30
00:01:46.284 --> 00:01:49.864
Any relevant later change invalidates that approval.

31
00:01:49.864 --> 00:01:54.094
Review is a deliberate action. never an automatic financial decision.

32
00:01:54.194 --> 00:02:01.076
The reviewer approves this snapshot. I open the packet.

33
00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:06.655
The reviewed packet includes the cash ledger. evidence. audit trail and snapshot hash.

34
00:02:06.655 --> 00:02:10.805
I can download it and verify that the hash matches the exact approved data.

35
00:02:10.905 --> 00:02:19.726
I download the packet and ledger. then reload the saved session.

36
00:02:19.866 --> 00:02:22.426
The reviewed session survives a reload.

37
00:02:22.426 --> 00:02:26.571
This is a readiness handoff. with no signatures or transfers.

38
00:02:26.571 --> 00:02:31.246
I built the concept to make rules. exceptions and human ownership clear.
